    "answer": {
      "short": "$864$\n\nUse inclusion–exclusion on the four same-colour adjacency events.",
      "worked": "Pens of the same colour are identical. For each colour, consider the event that its two pens are adjacent. Count intersections by treating each required adjacent pair as one block.\n\nLet $S_k$ be the sum of counts obtained by requiring adjacency for each selection of $k$ colours; $S_0$ counts all arrangements.\n$$\\begin{align*}S_0&=\\frac{8!}{(2!)^4}=2520\\\\S_1&=4\\times\\frac{7!}{(2!)^3}=2520\\\\S_2&=6\\times\\frac{6!}{(2!)^2}=1080\\\\S_3&=4\\times\\frac{5!}{2!}=240\\\\S_4&=4!=24.\\end{align*}$$\nSubtracting $S_1$ removes arrangements with a same-colour pair together. An arrangement with two such pairs has been subtracted twice, so $S_2$ restores it once. Overlaps involving three or four pairs need further alternating corrections. More generally, an arrangement with $r$ adjacent same-colour pairs has total weight $\\sum_{k=0}^{r}(-1)^k\\binom{r}{k}=(1-1)^r$. This weight is $0$ when $r>0$, and $1$ when $r=0$, so only the permitted arrangements remain.\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=2520-2520+1080-240+24\\\\N&=864.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
